# 1Password env-file template — `op run --env-file=.env.op -- <cmd>` resolves
# the op:// references to actual secret values and injects them as env vars
# for the wrapped command. Values never appear in shell scrollback or argv.
#
# This file IS committed (it contains references, not secrets). Anyone with
# read access to the Goldberry Grove - Admin vault's Grove Infra
# item gets the values; anyone without it gets `op` errors and nothing leaks.

# Provider credentials (read by TF as TF_VAR_*)
TF_VAR_do_token=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/do_token

# ACCOUNT-scoped Cloudflare token (DNS + Zone read + Zone Settings + SSL and
# Certificates edit on all four brand zones). The SSL permission authorizes
# cloudflare_origin_ca_certificate - Cloudflare deprecated the legacy Origin
# CA Key, so origin certs issue via this token too.
TF_VAR_cloudflare_api_token=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/account_cloudflare_api_token

# Spaces "plumbing" key (All Buckets) — provider-side bucket ops ONLY.
# The droplet gets its own TF-created bucket-scoped key (blogs.tf); this
# one never lands on a droplet.
TF_VAR_spaces_access_id=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/spaces_bootstrap_access_key_id
TF_VAR_spaces_secret_key=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/spaces_bootstrap_secret_key

# S3 backend auth (read by the AWS SDK that the TF S3 backend uses for Spaces)
AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/spaces_bootstrap_access_key_id
AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/spaces_bootstrap_secret_key

# --- App Platform frontends (GOL-116 / GOL-286) -----------------------------
# LIVE as of 2026-07-26 (GOL-817 App Platform apply). All three fields exist in
# Grove Infra (Admin vault):
#   * grove_revalidate_secret:    32-byte hex, shared across all 4 apps.
#   * odoo_api_keys_tf_json:      JSON map {"goldberry":..,"ggg":..,"nursery":..},
#                                 global-scope res.users.apikeys on the PROD Odoo.
#   * ghost_content_keys_tf_json: JSON map {"hub":..,"goldberry":..,"ggg":..,
#                                 "nursery":..}, assembled from the per-blog
#                                 ghost_content_key_* fields (GOL-817).
TF_VAR_grove_revalidate_secret=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/grove_revalidate_secret
TF_VAR_odoo_api_keys=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/odoo_api_keys_tf_json
TF_VAR_ghost_content_keys=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/ghost_content_keys_tf_json

# Discord #grove-ops paging webhook for the platform-plane alerts (GOL-381).
# observability.tf appends Discord's `/slack` Slack-compat suffix itself.
TF_VAR_discord_webhook_url=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/discord_webhook_url

# --- Nightly backup dead-man's switches -> self-hosted obs stack (GOL-855) ----
# Board decision 3a05a48b (2026-07-27): the backup heartbeats go to the
# self-hosted obs stack (grove-obs OpenObserve + Keep), NOT Healthchecks.io and
# NOT left unmonitored. This SUPERSEDES the Healthchecks.io arming steps that
# #301 documented here. The var NAMES keep the `healthchecks` prefix only to
# avoid a churny cross-file rename; the VALUES are now obs-stack ingest URLs.
#
# The value is the OpenObserve JSON-ingest endpoint for the `backup_heartbeat`
# stream, with basic-auth creds embedded in the URL, e.g.:
#   https://<oo-ingest-user>:<oo-ingest-pass>@<grove-obs-host>:5080/api/default/backup_heartbeat/_json
# The backup script POSTs a {job,stamp,...} record on success; an OpenObserve
# absence alert (openobserve/alerts.json: odoo-filestore-backup-stale-critical /
# blogs-backup-stale-warning) fires to Discord via Keep when no heartbeat lands
# in ~25h. One heartbeat job per backup so a green blogs beat can't mask a dead
# Odoo backup.
#
# BLOCKED on GOL-381: the prod droplets can only reach grove-obs:5080 once the
# prod->obs ingress exists (ingest_source_cidrs allow + reachable endpoint).
# Both backups currently default to "" (UNMONITORED) until armed. To arm:
#   1. Provision a scoped OpenObserve ingest token/user on grove-obs (least
#      privilege: write-only to the `backup_heartbeat` stream).
#   2. Store the full ingest URLs in 1P:
#        op item edit "Grove Infra" --vault "Goldberry Grove - Admin" \
#          odoo_backup_heartbeat_ingest_url="https://.../backup_heartbeat/_json" \
#          blogs_backup_heartbeat_ingest_url="https://.../backup_heartbeat/_json"
#      (may be the SAME endpoint — the job is set per-droplet in cloud-init.)
#   3. Uncomment both lines below and apply. NOTE: the URL is baked into each
#      droplet's cloud-init user_data, so arming FORCES A DROPLET REPLACE
#      (production-affecting — board-approved window; durable volumes survive,
#      validated on QA L3 under GOL-825).
#   4. Verify: confirm a real heartbeat row lands in `backup_heartbeat`, then
#      simulate a miss and confirm the absence alert pages Discord (GOL-855 §3).
# TF_VAR_odoo_backup_healthchecks_ping_url=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/odoo_backup_heartbeat_ingest_url
# TF_VAR_healthchecks_ping_url=op://Goldberry Grove - Admin/Grove Infra/blogs_backup_heartbeat_ingest_url
